IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfac-239`

-- Assertions written by an independent reader of Cut A (group 4, a fresh agent that wrote its answers from the text before it opened any encoding),
-- kept here where the encoding was changed to agree with the reader. Each carries the reader's scenario number and the answer the reader expected.
-- The reader's scenario #52 caught a naming defect: the functions for s 239(3A)(a) and (b) were named with "not" ("is not an offer of debentures", "is not a debenture") and answered JUST FALSE for the cases the text names,
-- so name and value read in opposite directions. They are now named `... is an offer of debentures` and `... is a debenture`, with the same values; the reader's #51 to #53 are recast to the new names.
-- The reader's answer to #51 and #52 is NO ("not an offer of debentures", "not a debenture"), which is JUST FALSE for a function that asks whether the invitation is an offer, or the document a debenture.

-- reader scenario #51, s 239(3A)(a) (text lines 37745-37747): a licensed bank invites a person to make a deposit with the bank: an offer of debentures? Expected NO.
-- arguments: the combined function takes what s 239(3)(a) answers for the invitation (TRUE: an invitation to lend, deemed an offer) and what s 239(3A)(a) answers (the body is a prescribed entity; the invitation is to make a deposit with it)
#ASSERT (`s 239(3) and (3A) the invitation to deposit or lend is an offer of debentures` (`s 239(3)(a) the invitation is deemed to be an offer of debentures of the entity` TRUE) (`s 239(3A)(a) the invitation by the prescribed entity is an offer of debentures` TRUE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- reader scenario #52, s 239(3A)(b) (text lines 37749-37752): a certificate of deposit issued by a licensed bank: a debenture? Expected NO.
-- arguments: the body is a prescribed entity; the document is issued by it; the document is a certificate of deposit; the document acknowledges a deposit (FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 239(3A)(b) the document issued by the prescribed entity is a debenture` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- reader scenario #53, s 239(3) and (3A): the same invitation made by a company that is not a prescribed entity: an offer of debentures? Expected YES (through s 239(3)(a)).
#ASSERT (`s 239(3) and (3A) the invitation to deposit or lend is an offer of debentures` (`s 239(3)(a) the invitation is deemed to be an offer of debentures of the entity` TRUE) (`s 239(3A)(a) the invitation by the prescribed entity is an offer of debentures` FALSE TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
